Quick summary of the Scheduling Classes

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCHED_RR / SCHED_FIFO:  realtimeish meaning if any task in this class has work it will preempt everybody else. The 
difference being SCHED_RR has a max timeslice concept whereas SCHED_FIFO will run until a higher priority takes its place

each of these tasks can have a static priority between 0 ~ 99 ( pretty cool eh ) btw higher the better 

<Q: not sure what happens to dynamic priority for SCHED_RR .. does it get modified by nice/usage pattern ?>

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCHED_NORMAL (or SCHED_OTHER) if you will is your regular round robin scheduling class.. it starts up with a static
priority of 0 (yep thats all that is allowed) and based on the nice value given and usage pattern its dynamic priority
changes. Initially there used to be the crazy multi level feedback loop concept like other OSes now its been changed
to include CFS (yes that is indeed very cool )

SCHED_BATCH not much clear but it appears that it behaves just like SCHED_NORMAL except when it wakes up something different
happens to this class based on the penalty (apparently tasks in this class get penalized higher than in SCHED_OTHER on 
wakeup)
